Improved: IBTK::PETScLevelSolver, IBTK::CCPoissonHypreLevelSolver, IBTK::SCPoissonHypreLevelSolver, and their library subclasses now reuse the data that depend only on the layout of the level. Examples are the DOF indices, the subdomain index sets, the hypre grid, and the cell- and side-centered matrix preallocation. The solvers reuse these data when initializeSolverState() initializes a solver that is already initialized and the level, the vectors, and the options are unchanged. They recompute only the matrices, preconditioners, and null spaces. IBAMR::StaggeredStokesPETScLevelSolver recomputes the Stokes matrix preallocation. IBTK::PETScKrylovLinearSolver and IBTK::PETScNewtonKrylovSolver now reuse their clones of the solution and right-hand-side vectors in that case.
<br>
